und to be 59.5%, whereas for papers over the replication rate was just 33.8% (see <a href=\"../assets/pdf/Bogdan_2025_PsyChange_Manuscript_SuppMat.pdf\">Supplemental Materials 7.3 of the mentioned paper</a>).","statement1":"As of 2020-2024, papers containing <span  \"><i>\"trimester\" </i></span> tend to be published in lower impact factor journals (<span style=\"color: rgba(105, 219, 99, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">27<sup>th</sup></span> percentile among all words)  but tend to be cited more (<span style=\"color: rgba(255, 168, 82, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">74<sup>th</sup></span> percentile word). In general, this word is positively associated with university ranking, such that higher-ranked institutions are more likely to publish papers containing <span  \"><i>\"trimester\" </i></span> (<span style=\"color: rgba(170, 117, 250, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">95<sup>th</sup></span> percentile). "}